{
 "_what": "LIB-REF-IN: the CALLER CLASSIFICATION half of the inbound adjudication -- what the fork does with each original function that calls a body libmh owns.",
 "_derived_vs_written": [
  "The caller SET is derived on every run by tools/gen_libmh_inbound.py (per-function ledgers +",
  "call_graph_no_crt.json, cut-free and all-domain -- see that tool's banner for why the",
  "reconciliation's section-5 cut is the WRONG model for this question). This file is the",
  "hand-written half: what CLASS each caller is. A caller with no row here FAILS the generator",
  "by name; a row here naming a caller that is no longer a caller FAILS as stale. Neither is",
  "silently defaulted, which is the failure docs/libmh-abi.md section 8 already demonstrated."
 ],
 "_classes": {
  "FE": "front-end (UI/HUD/menu/dialog/input/selection/camera/render/sound/debug console/frame loop) -- the fork's host reimplements it, so its call into an owned body needs a designed entry",
  "NET": "transport/lockstep driver -- host-side at the fork (mh_common/net_transport.cpp), so its call into an owned body needs a designed entry",
  "SESSION": "boot/session orchestration -- host-side at the fork, so its call into an owned body needs a designed lifecycle entry",
  "DRIVER": "the sim tick driver -- at the fork this IS libmh_sim_step, so the edge is absorbed by the spine rather than exported",
  "BOOT": "cfg/map parser -- reimplemented host-side post-fork (docs/endgame-plan.md D-E5); the state it produces crosses as libmh_import_snapshot / libmh_import_world",
  "TL": "original sim/logic code a later translation batch absorbs -- the edge dissolves with its caller and implies no inbound API"
 },
